<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35485" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per-sentisco</span></b> , ĕre, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>v. intens. a.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To perceive clearly</i>, <i>to
			detect</i> (ante-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nunc ne legio persentiscat, clam illuc
					redeundum'st mihi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Am. 1, 3, 28</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Aul. 1, 1, 24</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ubi possem persentiscere, Ni essem lapis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Heaut. 5, 1, 43</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To feel deeply</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">viscera persentiscunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
				3</span></i>
			 (249). </div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
